WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.620
You see, this desert is where...

3
00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.880
...you'll die!

4
00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.220
Un. Deux. Ora!

5
00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.260
Karoo!

6
00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:10.520
<b>Molehill Zone Four</b>

7
00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.240
Oh, no.

8
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.000
You see, you two...

9
00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.240
...can't get away. Swan Dash!

10
00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:29.920
You hear me?

11
00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.620
There's no escape for you!

12
00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.260
Just give up now, okay?

13
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.760
I'm going to trample you
both with all the grace

14
00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.930
of a ballerina.

15
00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.430
Karoo.

16
00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.400
You saved my life.

17
00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.700
You're in no shape
to be running like this now.

18
00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.380
No! If you go straight,

19
00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.380
we'll be cornered
on the stairway!

20
00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:03.910
Fools, listen to me!

21
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.050
Just give it up and stop right there!

22
00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.280
Let me off here.

23
00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:09.780
I'm going to fight him.

24
00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.720
What are you doing?
That way's a cliff.

25
00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:21.060
Oh! What are you doing?

26
00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.410
You can't be serious!

27
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.020
That duck is actually running
up the sheer face of a cliff?

28
00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.260
Huh?

29
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.130
Dumb duck!

30
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.040
Nice try, but now you'll
fall back down here

31
00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:49.040
and my Ballet Kenpo
will finish you off.

32
00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:57.860
How'd he do that?!

33
00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.100
Karoo, that's amazing! You flew!

34
00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:04.770
Surely Mr. 2 won't
be able to follow us

35
00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:05.970
at this point.

36
00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.640
That was a cute
little move, duck,

37
00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.680
but it's no use!

38
00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.450
There's nothing I can't do!

39
00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.480
With the help of my
incredible Ballet Kenpo,

40
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.780
I can relevé right
up this cliff.

41
00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.360
Karoo.

42
00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:32.960
Do you think you can make
it through the battlefield?

43
00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.340
We'll never be able to find Koza in all this confusion,

44
00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.970
so we'll look for Chaka instead.

45
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.100
We need to reach the royal palace.

46
00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.840
And we have to make it
before the rebel army

47
00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.980
reaches the center of the city.
We must!

48
00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.880
Oh, my. I'm here!

49
00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:03.870
A stray bullet, oh, no! Karoo!

50
00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.010
Vivi is our friend
too, 'kay, Karoo?

51
00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:15.830
Ah! Got ya!

52
00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:31.580
Karoo!

53
00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.020
Karoo!

54
00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.680
Just give up!

55
00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.890
I told you, it's no use!

56
00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.430
All right.

57
00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:11.020
Stay out of my way, duckie,

58
00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.790
and maybe you
won't get hurt, okay?

59
00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.200
No, stop!

60
00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.080
It's you guys.

61
00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:42.020
Nice work there, Captain Karoo.

62
00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.450
You did a damn good job.

63
00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.540
Oh! Sanji, you're here!

64
00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.900
At ease, ducks.
You can stand down.

65
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.840
Now, Vivi, don't you
have a rebellion to stop?

66
00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:01.180
Go on.

67
00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:03.210
I'll take care of this creep.

68
00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.240
So I take it
you're that ridiculous,

69
00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.510
face-changing freak, huh?

70
00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:13.910
You really should
stay out of my way.

71
00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:15.780
But first, just who are you?

72
00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:18.250
Go on.

73
00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:20.950
You guys, watch Karoo.

74
00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.660
Ah! No! She's getting away!

75
00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.300
Oh! You gotta be kidding me!

76
00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:34.830
Gimme a break here!

77
00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.740
Well... Now you get to die!

78
00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.670
I think I'll get started
by having you return

79
00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:41.640
our sharpshooter's
prized goggles.

80
00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.080
And that's just the beginning.

81
00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.330
Huh?

82
00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.040
Hope you didn't think
I would be as easy

83
00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.410
to beat as him.

84
00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.080
You're with the straw hats, huh?

85
00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:56.750
Well, then, that must make
you the mysterious prince.

86
00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.450
My name is Sanji,
and I'm the best cook

87
00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:03.920
in the entire ocean.

88
00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:08.330
Cook? I happen to be
a super first-class

89
00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.790
top-rate cook as well.

90
00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.930
But I use my skills to support
an underworld organization,

91
00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.760
not some useless kingdom.

92
00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.980
You're not the only one
who knows the underworld.

93
00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.780
I happen to be a cook and a pirate.

94
00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.010
Hmm.

95
00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.420
Well then, this should
be quite interesting.

96
00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:26.790
I'll make this clear.

97
00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.690
Keep your hands off this country.

98
00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:32.920
<b>Southeast Gate, Alubarna</b>

99
00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.450
Where's Chopper?

100
00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.220
Chopper!

101
00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.120
Chopper! Hey, Chopper!

102
00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.800
Come on, wake up!
Open your eyes!

103
00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:47.200
Oh, Usopp.

104
00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.220
It looks like you're
all right. That's great.

105
00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.720
Don't be ridiculous.

106
00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.490
You're the one we need to worry about.

107
00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.490
No, it isn't serious.

108
00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:55.890
So.

109
00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:58.730
This is all that's left
of the Mr. 4 pair, huh?

110
00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.130
And here I came to help you!

111
00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:01.780
I, the great Captain Usopp,

112
00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.090
the champion of the seas, the hero of the world,

113
00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.920
was going to demonstrate
my fighting skills

114
00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:08.160
by bravely coming
to a friend's rescue.

115
00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.830
Be careful, they're still
here waiting for us.

116
00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.560
What?! Why didn't you say so?

117
00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:22.480
What was that?

118
00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:25.480
How did that happen?
There's no one even out there!

119
00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:27.350
That's because they're underground.

120
00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.980
Miss Merry Christmas ate
the Mole-Mole Devil Fruit,

121
00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.420
and now she's a mole woman.

122
00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.050
A mole woman?

123
00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.180
The other one,

124
00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:38.440
Mr. 4, is a fourth batter,
and his dog's the pitcher.

125
00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.880
What? None of that jibber
jabber made any sense.

126
00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.040
What the hell does it mean?

127
00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:48.020
Look out!

128
00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.290
Four!

129
00:09:55.800 --> 00:10:01.830
<b>Mr. 4 & Miss Merry Christmas
vs
Usopp & Chopper</b>

130
00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.680
Are you okay, Usopp?

131
00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.300
Man. That was really close!

132
00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:18.000
I'm glad you were there, Chopper.

133
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.240
What exactly was
that thing anyway?

134
00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.310
Like I said.

135
00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:24.710
That's Mr. 4's thing.
He's a fourth batter.

136
00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:26.410
He works together with his dog.

137
00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.080
Which brings me back to my earlier point.

138
00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:29.520
None of that makes any sense.

139
00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.390
Ah! Look, he's over there!

140
00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:34.410
A dog?

141
00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.980
Gah! What is that weird thing?

142
00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.150
That's not good!

143
00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.160
What? Huh? What's that?

144
00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:54.490
Here it comes!

145
00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:55.690
Not good!

146
00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.130
Four!

147
00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.840
Usopp, you have to get away from there quickly!

148
00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:05.970
Hurry, now!

149
00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:15.090
Usopp, no!

150
00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.700
Are you all right, Usopp?

151
00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:27.170
Okay, one more time.
What is that?

152
00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:28.560
The ball is a time bomb.

153
00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:31.230
It explodes when it's set to,
whether or not it hits anything.

154
00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.560
Basically, Mr. 4 can
calculate the time needed

155
00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:34.900
and then hit the ball.

156
00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:37.330
The ball will then explode when its time is up.

157
00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:38.870
I tried to catch one before it exploded

158
00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.070
and throw it back at him,
but it's as heavy

159
00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:42.300
as a wrecking ball.

160
00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.150
There's no way to catch it and it's impossible to throw.

161
00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:46.830
The fact that Mr. 4
can hit it with a bat

162
00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.730
at the speed he does
is absolutely incredible.

163
00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:51.420
His strength is extraordinary.

164
00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.520
It's beyond anything I've ever seen before.

165
00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:57.590
Four.

166
00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:05.870
Lassoo...

167
00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:08.170
That bat of his just knocked down a brick wall.

168
00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.400
How much could that thing possibly weigh?

169
00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:14.070
Hey! Mr. 4! Mr. 4!

170
00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:15.570
What are you doing, moron?

171
00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:16.610
You moron!

172
00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:19.280
Go and get 'em instead
of just standing there!

173
00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:22.900
Come on let 'em have it already!
Go now! Go on, moron! Kill 'em!

174
00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:27.740
Smoke 'em! Blow 'em up!
Moron. Moron. Ron. Ron. Ron.

175
00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:30.270
Now! Do it now!

176
00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.380
Uh...

177
00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:33.800
Over there!
It's the mole woman!

178
00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:34.870
She is a mole!

179
00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:38.850
I haven't even changed yet,
you... ron, you moron.

180
00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.750
Chopper. You'll have
to take it from here.

181
00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.820
Do me a favor and have
my body buried at sea

182
00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:43.920
when I'm gone, okay?

183
00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:44.990
You cowardly jerk!

184
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.640
You just got done saying
you had come here to help!

185
00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:48.840
Look here, you!

186
00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:51.300
How do you expect me to fight
against a freaky muscle man,

187
00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:53.770
his weird dog-gun hybrid,
and a mole woman?

188
00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:55.770
There's no way! I'm a human!

189
00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:57.610
Do you think you can understand that?

190
00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:59.280
I'm a human too, jerk!

191
00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:01.280
No, you're not!
You're a big, furry monster!

192
00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:03.580
What about you? Have you
seen that nose of yours?

193
00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.700
Anyway, his name is Lassoo.

194
00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:07.340
He's a gun that ate
the dachshund variety

195
00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.670
of the Mutt-Mutt Fruit.

196
00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.210
Are we clear?

197
00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.610
Let me get this straight.

198
00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:14.880
Are you saying that
a gun ate a Devil Fruit?

199
00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.250
It's a new technique here in the Grand Line.

200
00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:20.250
Even inanimate objects can eat a devil fruit.

201
00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:21.800
Ha! You call that lying.

202
00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:24.460
If he was originally a gun, how could he eat anything?

203
00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:25.920
A gun can't even
move on its own.

204
00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:28.630
You're just making all of this up, you mole woman!

205
00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:29.780
Shut up!

206
00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:31.780
It's top secret, anyway,
and I wouldn't have told you

207
00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:34.620
except for you're going to die!
A gun can't help it if it moves!

208
00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:36.720
So there, there, there!
There! So there!

209
00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.290
Now, isn't that right, Mr. 4?

210
00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.450
Mm-hmm.

211
00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:42.620
Anyway, like I was saying,

212
00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:43.750
you're gonna die here.

213
00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:45.210
You have no hope of escaping

214
00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:46.610
now that you've
entered our territory.

215
00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:49.380
Nope, nuh-uh. No hope at all!

216
00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.360
You should enjoy this.

217
00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:53.090
Welcome to a territory
we call Molehill, Block 4.

218
00:13:58.530 --> 00:13:59.600
Look!

219
00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:02.030
Now she's turning into a
mole-woman-thing for real!

220
00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.370
Penguin?

221
00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:10.710
Not a penguin, I'm a mole!
Now, you shut up!

222
00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:16.480
She's underground.

223
00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:19.520
– Now's my chance!
– Wait, hey!

224
00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.280
You can handle
it from here, I'm sure!

225
00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.420
Watch out, Usopp!

226
00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:28.460
It missed!

227
00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:29.520
Close!

228
00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.030
Four!

229
00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:33.860
Oh, no!

230
00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.590
Usopp, look! It's above you!

231
00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.340
It's a fly ball!

232
00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:40.180
Ha! No problem!

233
00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:41.780
Looks like their cleanup
batter can't clean up

234
00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:43.250
very well, huh?

235
00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:45.590
How sad.

236
00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:47.630
I could dodge this one with my eyes closed!

237
00:14:48.890 --> 00:14:49.900
Spin ball!

238
00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.900
Look out behind you!

239
00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:58.440
He's fourth in our line-up

240
00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:01.740
for a reason, moron.
You haven't seen anything yet!

241
00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.350
They're over there!

242
00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:29.350
How did you two have the time to move?

243
00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:34.520
You changed form.

244
00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:36.620
All right, so you're
a Zoan type.

245
00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.560
And I was thinking you
were just a normal person

246
00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:39.690
all this time.

247
00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:43.060
Usopp, we have no choice but to keep moving.

248
00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:45.400
If we stop for a second, we're dead.

249
00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:46.400
I get it.

250
00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:48.070
If we stand still, then
we're just sitting ducks

251
00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:49.540
for them to keep firing at.

252
00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.040
Here they come!

253
00:15:57.340 --> 00:15:58.380
Four!

254
00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.920
If I can get to that guy
and knock him down...

255
00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.260
Just hold on!

256
00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:13.470
The game isn't going to be any fun

257
00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.440
if we don't have a batter, now is it?

258
00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:21.640
Chopper!

259
00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:28.920
Whew! Well, at least
I can still do that.

260
00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:31.400
Dirty mole!

261
00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:34.060
Bastard!

262
00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:40.540
Damn, if they keep running away
through these mole tunnels,

263
00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:42.910
even if I use a rumble ball,
I won't have enough time

264
00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.410
to do any real damage.

265
00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.650
Hey, where is he?

266
00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:50.650
Huh?

267
00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.090
We're missing one of 'em!
Where'd the ugly guy

268
00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.420
with the long nose
run off to?

269
00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.560
Where is he? Where?

270
00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:58.320
Yeah. I don't see Usopp
around anywhere.

271
00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.660
What's the matter?
You guys lose something?

272
00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.050
Where are you?

273
00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:05.410
Where did you go?

274
00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:07.880
Wait, is he...?

275
00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.690
Yep! So kind of you to
dig all these tunnels, really.

276
00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:12.460
You do realize, though,

277
00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:13.960
that you're not the
only one who can crawl

278
00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:15.360
around inside them.

279
00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.030
Usopp...!

280
00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.720
You sneaky little rat!

281
00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:23.370
You were hiding
in one of the holes.

282
00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:26.080
...Pound!

283
00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:39.050
Mr. 4!

284
00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:44.650
What?!

285
00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.900
It looks like he's using
a five-ton hammer!

286
00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:49.900
How does a string bean like him
have the strength to do that?

287
00:17:57.780 --> 00:17:59.640
That's a big hammer.

288
00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:01.980
Who exactly is this
long-nosed freak?

289
00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.650
I am a traveler
of the world's oceans.

290
00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:09.590
A crusher of notorious monsters,
beasts, and foes.

291
00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.160
A sinker of countless ships.

292
00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.080
A flattener of numberless towns.

293
00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:14.850
Trembling with fear,
people everywhere

294
00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:17.900
call me the master
of destruction! Heh heh.

295
00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:19.800
I suggest that you take
the time to remember

296
00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.090
my name carefully.

297
00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:25.460
I am... Captain Usopp!

298
00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:29.000
Wow! Wow! Wow! Awesome! Awesome!

299
00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.570
Yes, yes, thank you very much.
Ah, it's nothing, really.

300
00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:33.440
I'll be signing autographs later.

301
00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:35.510
I thought you
were useless up until now!

302
00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:38.540
Hey!

303
00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:39.740
Mr. 4...

304
00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:42.570
He isn't moving.

305
00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.710
Could I have really hit him that hard?

306
00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.570
No, it doesn't matter.

307
00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:48.480
This is my chance to beat them both.

308
00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:50.510
I have to take it.

309
00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:52.480
Your turn, penguin!

310
00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:55.620
Now you'll feel the wrath
of my five-ton hammer!

311
00:18:56.980 --> 00:19:00.720
Taste my Usopp Pound!

312
00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:04.430
She escaped.
Where are you, penguin?

313
00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:06.660
I told you! I'm a mole,
not a penguin, moron!

314
00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.760
Now I see you!

315
00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:09.760
Pound! Pound! Pound! Pound!

316
00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:12.030
Here! Here! Here! Here!

317
00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:13.580
– Pound! Pound! Pound! Pound!
– Here! Here! Here! Here!

318
00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:16.320
Damn!

319
00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.430
Damn, you're
everywhere, mole woman!

320
00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:27.500
Ha! Hey, ya missed me,
so what's the point

321
00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.500
of that big hammer

322
00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.640
if you can't
manage to hit me?

323
00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:34.600
Let me tell you
something, penguin.

324
00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:37.940
I'm sure you've heard
by now that a good number

325
00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:39.780
of your fellow
Baroque Works agents

326
00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:41.510
have been eliminated by us.

327
00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:46.620
But the truth is it was all me!

328
00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:47.650
You did all that?

329
00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:50.150
And in addition to that...

330
00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:52.490
I command eight thousand men!

331
00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:57.930
That's awesome!

332
00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:06.770
Rubber band of doom.

333
00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:12.630
– Five tons!
– Awesome!

334
00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.540
Ah! He has to wake up now?

335
00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:17.040
He survived being
hit by a five-ton hammer?

336
00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.010
What kind of monster is he?

337
00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:20.580
Yeah. He doesn't even
have a bump

338
00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.240
on his head.

339
00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:25.050
He took a direct blow to the
head from a five-ton hammer

340
00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.680
and he's okay? Why is that?

341
00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:36.320
Four?

342
00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:39.630
You mean that thing was a fake?

343
00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:41.230
This whole time?

344
00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.730
Of course it was!

345
00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.730
You think I can really lift five tons?

346
00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:47.070
I stop trying after
just 10 pounds!

347
00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.800
This is a model I made.

348
00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:51.770
<b>Support</b>
<b>Fittings</b>
<b>(0.5kg)</b>
<b>Miscellaneous</b>
<b>(0.1kg)</b>
<b>Black Plastic</b>
<b>(thick)</b>
<b>Usopp Hammer, Edition S</b>
<b>5t (false label)</b>
<b>Usopp Pound</b>
<b>Frying Pan
(0.7kg)</b>

349
00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:51.560
<b>Weight: 2kg</b>

350
00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.970
It's only a couple of
frying pans tied to a stick

351
00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:52.240
and covered with paper.

352
00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.540
Why, you...

353
00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.900
You tricked me with
a piece of paper?

354
00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:04.240
No more mercy for you!

355
00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:08.140
Mole Swimming!

356
00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:09.760
Mole fish escape!

357
00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:13.930
She's gone underground
into the mole tunnels again.

358
00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:15.870
Watch out for the holes, Chopper!

359
00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:18.510
What's she planning this time?

360
00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.180
Moving around underground
is just like

361
00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:21.980
swimming in a pool to me.

362
00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:23.820
You can't escape this time!

363
00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:29.190
Pool?

364
00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:35.360
Now this is bad.

365
00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:37.100
Mole-mole!

366
00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:38.130
Usopp!

367
00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:40.540
Banana!

368
00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:45.360
Mr. 4. Lassoo.

369
00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:47.260
Go ahead and take care
of that reindeer man

370
00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:49.590
– over there, would ya?
– Four!

371
00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:52.200
Let's show them your
Four Hundred Base Knocks!

372
00:21:59.270 --> 00:22:00.270
It's no use.

373
00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:03.600
There's no way I can
handle an attack like this.

374
00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.230
It's all or nothing now.

375
00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:07.470
I have to think up
a way to beat this guy,

376
00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:10.070
and quickly,
before he kills us both!

377
00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:13.410
Rumble!

378
00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:20.580
Brain Point!

379
00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:30.420
Scope!

380
00:22:37.610 --> 00:22:38.810
Where's Chopper?

381
00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:44.730
Chopper.

382
00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:47.830
You don't have time
to be worried about

383
00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:49.000
someone else!

384
00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:55.920
Here comes my mole banana!

385
00:22:57.920 --> 00:22:59.460
Hey, now. What are you doing?

386
00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:01.860
It's poor form to go after that spot on a guy!

387
00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:04.730
Stop your whining!
You're alive, aren't you?

388
00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:08.640
Mole Banana!
Banana! Banana! Banana!

389
00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:12.390
Banana! Banana! Banana!
Banana! Banana! Banana!

390
00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:13.740
Perfect!

391
00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:15.260
There's part of a wall there!

392
00:23:15.260 --> 00:23:17.500
If I keep running at this speed and she follows me,

393
00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:20.600
she'll run into the part of
the wall that's under the sand!

394
00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:23.670
And she'll crash really hard, too!

395
00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:25.570
Banana! Banana!

396
00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:29.110
Come on! Come on!
Come on! Come on!

397
00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:30.610
Now it's time to split
your head in two,

398
00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:31.940
stupid penguin!

399
00:23:54.670 --> 00:23:56.400
back on the ship.

400
00:23:56.440 --> 00:23:57.510
Right now...

401
00:23:57.570 --> 00:24:00.580
I just have to do
whatever I can!

402
00:24:28.370 --> 00:24:29.600
Hi-ya!

403
00:24:32.670 --> 00:24:33.710
Hi-ya!

404
00:24:41.150 --> 00:24:42.320
Got crushed, huh?

405
00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:44.620
Well it serves you right, you
stupid old penguin woman!

406
00:24:44.650 --> 00:24:46.860
A mole!
I'm a mole, you moron!

407
00:24:47.890 --> 00:24:49.120
Molehill Highway!

408
00:24:52.830 --> 00:24:55.200
What are you doing?
Let me go!

409
00:24:55.230 --> 00:24:57.730
Stop it, already! This is
too dangerous to do out here!

410
00:24:57.730 --> 00:24:59.400
If you're not careful, we'll run into something!

411
00:24:59.400 --> 00:25:01.170
Ahh! Like that wall
in front of you!

412
00:25:01.200 --> 00:25:03.370
Look ahead! A wall, a wall!

413
00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:06.380
Help! I'm too young to die!

414
00:25:06.410 --> 00:25:08.740
Mole-mole Impact!

415
00:25:19.090 --> 00:25:21.760
I got it!
I see your weakness now!

416
00:25:31.190 --> 00:25:32.420
Now!

417
00:25:47.070 --> 00:25:48.740
Usopp!

418
00:25:48.810 --> 00:25:50.080
Usopp, can you get up?

419
00:25:50.080 --> 00:25:52.680
Come on, Usopp!

420
00:25:52.710 --> 00:25:54.880
Stay away from the mole and all the holes, too!

421
00:25:56.750 --> 00:25:58.880
You don't have to tell me twice!
I'm going!

422
00:26:00.220 --> 00:26:01.420
Hurry up!

423
00:26:01.430 --> 00:26:03.930
What exactly are those morons doing now?

424
00:26:27.460 --> 00:26:28.790
What's that?

425
00:26:42.370 --> 00:26:45.240
And that's the
molehill's weakness.

426
00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.310
All of the tunnels are
connected to each other

427
00:26:47.310 --> 00:26:48.810
in one big network.

428
00:26:49.980 --> 00:26:50.980
Oh?

429
00:26:53.150 --> 00:26:54.320
Yeah?

430
00:27:08.480 --> 00:27:09.620
They're alive?

431
00:27:09.650 --> 00:27:10.880
This isn't good!

432
00:27:10.880 --> 00:27:12.650
My Rumble Ball's
effectiveness is already

433
00:27:12.690 --> 00:27:13.990
half-gone by now!

434
00:27:18.560 --> 00:27:19.790
No more.

435
00:27:19.850 --> 00:27:21.090
Huh?

436
00:27:21.120 --> 00:27:24.360
No more of this!
I don't wanna die in this place!

437
00:27:24.390 --> 00:27:25.190
Usopp, wait!

438
00:27:25.220 --> 00:27:27.030
No way, I'm outta here!
I've had it!

439
00:27:27.060 --> 00:27:28.750
There's no way to beat these two!

440
00:27:28.750 --> 00:27:31.370
Not when they're still alive after that explosion!

441
00:27:31.370 --> 00:27:32.870
Running away from
them isn't going to do

442
00:27:32.910 --> 00:27:34.510
any good, don't you see?

443
00:27:36.250 --> 00:27:37.390
Usopp!

444
00:27:37.420 --> 00:27:39.260
The Blue nose is right, you know.

445
00:27:41.660 --> 00:27:44.230
That was quite
a little stunt you pulled!

446
00:27:44.260 --> 00:27:45.430
After doing something like that,

447
00:27:45.460 --> 00:27:46.830
we're not gonna just
let you run away

448
00:27:46.870 --> 00:27:48.770
like nothing happened.

449
00:27:48.810 --> 00:27:50.380
Oh, no! Usopp!

450
00:27:55.610 --> 00:27:57.520
Well, I guess with a
captain who's so pathetic,

451
00:27:57.580 --> 00:28:00.020
it's no surprise that the
rest of the crew's useless.

452
00:28:05.020 --> 00:28:07.020
Captain? Wait.

453
00:28:07.020 --> 00:28:09.830
Are you...
Are you talking about Luffy?

454
00:28:09.860 --> 00:28:11.530
If you're talking
about the Straw Hat kid,

455
00:28:11.550 --> 00:28:13.780
that idiot was killed a little
while ago by the boss.

456
00:28:13.810 --> 00:28:15.420
What a shocker.

457
00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:18.880
And now the rebellion has
started and is well under way.

458
00:28:18.890 --> 00:28:20.820
Well. I guess you
picked the wrong people

459
00:28:20.890 --> 00:28:21.890
to mess with.

460
00:28:29.130 --> 00:28:31.630
She said Luffy is dead?

461
00:28:35.070 --> 00:28:37.440
Don't you dare lie to us!

462
00:28:38.630 --> 00:28:40.670
Don't lie to us,
you dirty mole woman!

463
00:28:40.670 --> 00:28:42.140
We aren't gonna listen to you!

464
00:28:42.170 --> 00:28:45.110
There's no way Luffy can
be dead, do you hear me?

465
00:28:45.140 --> 00:28:48.180
He'd never lose to that alligator bastard!

466
00:28:48.240 --> 00:28:49.810
And what makes you
think that scrawny

467
00:28:49.810 --> 00:28:51.750
little captain of yours
could even last five seconds

468
00:28:51.780 --> 00:28:53.980
against our boss?
You stupid long nose!

469
00:28:53.980 --> 00:28:55.790
Because someday
he's going to become

470
00:28:55.790 --> 00:28:57.670
the King of the Pirates!

471
00:28:57.670 --> 00:29:00.670
So there's no chance that he would let himself die here!

472
00:29:03.840 --> 00:29:05.610
Did you hear that, Mr. 4?

473
00:29:05.640 --> 00:29:08.640
He'll be the pirate king.
Pi king. Pi king.

474
00:29:08.640 --> 00:29:10.880
That's the stupidest thing I've ever heard!

475
00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:22.720
King of the Pirates!
Only idiots like you

476
00:29:22.720 --> 00:29:24.060
and your pathetic friends
would believe

477
00:29:24.060 --> 00:29:26.560
a ridiculous story like that.

478
00:29:26.560 --> 00:29:28.800
I'm glad that pathetic
captain of yours is dead.

479
00:29:28.830 --> 00:29:31.570
He was a moron who
didn't know his own place.

480
00:29:31.570 --> 00:29:35.970
He was a 'ron! 
A 'ron!

481
00:29:42.880 --> 00:29:44.700
Chopper! Listen!

482
00:29:44.700 --> 00:29:47.070
A real man...

483
00:29:49.700 --> 00:29:52.630
It's about time
you die, long nose!

484
00:29:52.630 --> 00:29:55.470
Molehill Highway!

485
00:29:55.470 --> 00:29:56.300
Listen to me.

486
00:29:56.300 --> 00:29:58.410
A real man,
no matter how terrifying

487
00:29:58.440 --> 00:30:00.640
or hideous or corrupt
his enemy might be...

488
00:30:01.740 --> 00:30:04.580
I'll see you in hell, 'ron,
ya long nosed 'ron!

489
00:30:06.480 --> 00:30:08.780
Mole-mole impact!

490
00:30:09.130 --> 00:30:09.900
You okay?!

491
00:30:11.550 --> 00:30:13.960
No... No matter
how slim the chance,

492
00:30:13.960 --> 00:30:16.130
a real man will still fight!

493
00:30:20.190 --> 00:30:21.330
Mr. 4!

494
00:30:23.330 --> 00:30:26.130
You're up!
Now take your batting stance!

495
00:30:26.170 --> 00:30:27.700
Ready your four-ton bat!

496
00:30:29.600 --> 00:30:30.800
This is it.

497
00:30:30.840 --> 00:30:32.610
Molehill...

498
00:30:41.820 --> 00:30:44.280
Intersection Number Four!

499
00:31:05.220 --> 00:31:06.460
The weak are always weak,

500
00:31:06.490 --> 00:31:07.960
even if they
pretend they're not.

501
00:31:07.990 --> 00:31:09.100
How sad.

502
00:31:11.460 --> 00:31:12.730
Damn you!

503
00:31:14.170 --> 00:31:16.100
What did you do to him?

504
00:31:24.940 --> 00:31:27.110
There are times when...

505
00:31:27.140 --> 00:31:30.250
When a real man
must stay and fight

506
00:31:30.280 --> 00:31:31.950
instead of running.

507
00:31:31.980 --> 00:31:33.150
No matter what.

508
00:31:34.560 --> 00:31:36.760
You're still standing?

509
00:31:38.160 --> 00:31:40.160
Like now,

510
00:31:40.220 --> 00:31:45.100
when a friend's true dream
is laughed at by someone.

511
00:31:45.190 --> 00:31:46.390
No way.

512
00:31:46.390 --> 00:31:49.200
You were hit in the head with a bat that weighs four tons!

513
00:31:49.230 --> 00:31:51.340
You shouldn't even
be alive, ya damn 'ron.

514
00:31:51.340 --> 00:31:54.140
You shouldn't, no ya shouldn't,
shouldn't even be alive, no way.

515
00:31:54.240 --> 00:31:56.840
What sort of sneaky trick are you using this time, huh?

516
00:31:58.810 --> 00:32:02.010
Luffy is not dead.

517
00:32:02.040 --> 00:32:05.580
He's going to be King
of the Pirates someday.

518
00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:09.810
I know he will!

519
00:32:12.020 --> 00:32:13.820
That is one thing

520
00:32:13.840 --> 00:32:16.610
that I will never let
you laugh at! Never!

521
00:32:16.660 --> 00:32:17.700
Ha!

522
00:32:17.790 --> 00:32:19.960
I guess the long nose hasn't
learned his lesson yet.

523
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:21.900
Let's go again, Mr. 4!

524
00:32:26.240 --> 00:32:27.970
I'm not gonna let that happen!

525
00:32:29.070 --> 00:32:31.040
Let me show you
a transformation point

526
